+# Codeware macOS arm64 port: engine bindings
+
+Target: Cyberpunk 2077 2.3.1, macOS arm64 (UUID A6656ADC-FBE2-36A4-9B9D-B4A9DE645089), Itanium C++ ABI.
+Rules: `../cp2077-archive-xl-macos/AGENTS.md`. macOS code is behind `#ifdef __APPLE__`; the Windows path is unchanged.
+
+## Conventions
+
+- Addresses resolve by hash through `lib/Support/macOS/ArchiveXLAddressResolver.cpp` to the RED4ext.SDK address DB.
+  Only entries marked verified resolve. Addresses come from the research files, not from this repo.
+- `Core::RawVFunc` offsets stay MSVC offsets in the source. `lib/Core/Raw.hpp` adds 8 on macOS (Itanium destructor
+  pair) and asserts the slot is after the destructor. Where MSVC grouped overloaded virtuals, the source offset is
+  changed so that offset + 8 is the checked macOS slot (see JournalManager).
+- Results that the game returns through x8 are declared as by-value returns of non-trivially-copyable types
+  (`Red::Handle`, `Red::SharedPtr`, `Red::WeakPtr`, `Red::SretValue<N>` in `src/Red/MacCompat.hpp`).
+  `src/App/Application.cpp` has static_asserts for the types used.
+- New hashes for macOS-only targets are FNV-1a 32 of the name (same scheme as ArchiveXL-macos).
+- Features that cannot be made safe are compiled out on macOS (fail closed): their hash constant is not in the binary,
+  script natives stay registered and return defaults, and `CODEWARE_MAC_UNSUPPORTED` logs once.
+
+Evidence keys: **boot** = `research/re_boot/results.md`, **cw** = `research/re_codeware/results.md`,
+**tri** = `research/re_codeware_triage/triage.md`, **ink** = `research/re_ink/results.md`,
+**med** = `research/re_medium/results.md`, **wl** = `research/codeware_port_worklist.md`,
+**port** = decompiles and notes in `research/re_codeware_port/` (this port), **gaps** = `research/re_codeware_gaps/results.md`,
+**sdk** = RED4ext.SDK `docs/re/*.md`.
+
